WEBVTT

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:13.180
Romeo's Blue Skies

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:12.820
"To the Sky..."

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:17.880
<i>Overlooking the rows of houses and stores</i>

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:22.290
<i>from the highest vantage,</i>

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:27.400
<i>Such things as tears and sadness</i>

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:31.540
<i>will quickly vanish</i>

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:37.100
<i>The birds, wind, and sunshine...</i>

00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:41.290
<i>...all are your friends</i>

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:46.360
<i>I'll carry this dream farther than far</i>

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:51.450
<i>...no matter the distance...</i>

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:58.210
<i>I long to fly freely</i>

00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:02.490
<i>through the blue sky in my heart...</i>

00:01:02.530 --> 00:01:05.420
<i>The far distant blue sky</i>

00:01:05.530 --> 00:01:12.870
<i>It flows into tomorrow</i>

00:01:20.390 --> 00:01:25.180
Takara Fansubs

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:32.360
<i>At long last, Romeo was reunited with Alfredo.</i>

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:38.200
<i>They joined forces with the other chimney sweeps,</i>

00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:40.360
<i>...forming "The Black Brothers" fraternity.</i>

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:48.030
<i>The boys gathered in a secret underground sanctuary,</i>

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:51.530
<i>...exchanging vows of courage and unity.</i>

00:01:51.730 --> 00:01:56.430
Episode 16:

00:01:51.730 --> 00:01:56.430
Alfredo is My Rival!

00:02:09.590 --> 00:02:11.240
Today was pretty rough!

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:25.610
Well, I'd better be...

00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:28.140
Uh? Michaelo!

00:02:31.690 --> 00:02:36.340
Today... at the secret hideout... a meeting...

00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:42.320
...of the Black Brothers...
everybody come!

00:02:43.570 --> 00:02:45.310
Right! I gotcha!

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:52.320
The question is...
Who'll charge into the Wolf Pack?

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:54.880
I told you... I'll do it!

00:02:55.010 --> 00:02:57.700
Romeo?!
- Are you serious?

00:02:57.990 --> 00:03:00.700
Yes. I'll punch through into the Wolf Pack.

00:03:01.070 --> 00:03:02.860
But you're already a veteran at being pounded by 'em!

00:03:04.670 --> 00:03:06.190
But... no! ...this time...!

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:08.130
No, it's best I go.

00:03:08.350 --> 00:03:09.080
Eh?!

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:11.590
I'm the bravest, after all.

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:12.840
The bravest!?

00:03:13.810 --> 00:03:16.350
The bravest!
- You must be joking!

00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:18.130
I'm the bravest!

00:03:18.710 --> 00:03:19.880
Says who!?
- I'm the bravest, I'm the bravest...!

00:03:19.890 --> 00:03:22.040
Stop it, Romeo, Augusto!

00:03:23.490 --> 00:03:27.520
Who cares who it is? Hurry up and decide, will you, or else I'm going home.

00:03:28.470 --> 00:03:30.060
Oh, Alfredo.

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:33.300
How long have you been here?

00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:40.200
Alfredo! Don't you agree it's me who should charge at them?

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:42.340
Tell them you think it's me, Alfredo!

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:46.170
Sure, but... there's more to consider than just that...

00:03:46.390 --> 00:03:47.450
...more to consider?

00:03:48.380 --> 00:03:50.580
Over there, each of them is a strongman.

00:03:51.090 --> 00:03:54.500
So one-by-one, we can't take them all on... don't you think?

00:03:59.110 --> 00:04:01.620
That's not at all like you.

00:04:02.110 --> 00:04:04.510
Romeo, let's listen to what our leader has to say.

00:04:18.770 --> 00:04:20.230
Here, have a bite to eat.

00:04:22.190 --> 00:04:23.710
All... All right.

00:04:30.920 --> 00:04:34.690
Everyone, the important thing, as I see it, is teamwork.

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:36.050
Teamwork...?

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:36.870
That's right.

00:04:38.260 --> 00:04:40.240
This is a map of the area.

00:04:41.610 --> 00:04:42.200
Now, listen.

00:04:43.130 --> 00:04:46.240
Tachioni jumps Michaelo at the same place each time.

00:04:47.930 --> 00:04:48.420
Right here.

00:04:48.700 --> 00:04:52.940
That's right... I was always jumped at the back of this bakery!

00:04:53.420 --> 00:04:57.210
The next time it happens, signal us by blowing on this.

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:05.060
Both Antonio and Augusto are in the area. And so am I.

00:05:05.460 --> 00:05:06.730
Somebody's bound to hear it.

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:11.830
Benalino...

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:15.930
...can you run over to notify Romeo?

00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:18.040
Notify Romeo?

00:05:18.640 --> 00:05:19.190
Right.

00:05:20.360 --> 00:05:22.450
Romeo and Dante are on the opposite side.

00:05:24.190 --> 00:05:26.260
They'll cover us from here.

00:05:26.370 --> 00:05:28.530
I hear ya... a pincer attack, eh?

00:05:30.010 --> 00:05:31.800
Romeo! Let's do it!

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:33.230
Uh, sure...

00:05:33.670 --> 00:05:36.730
I see...! No matter how tough Tachioni is,

00:05:36.890 --> 00:05:38.720
...we just need to get him surrounded!

00:05:40.330 --> 00:05:41.430
That's right!

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:44.180
There's nothing to be scared of, this way!

00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:50.490
Actually, geographically, this area gives us the advantage.

00:05:50.820 --> 00:05:52.620
So I'm almost positive the plan will succeed.

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:54.080
Any other ones?

00:05:54.630 --> 00:05:57.140
You've got alternate plans, don't you?

00:05:57.720 --> 00:05:59.850
It might drag on for a bit...
but... are you ready?

00:06:00.010 --> 00:06:00.820
Of course!

00:06:01.350 --> 00:06:02.870
Tell us, Alfredo!

00:06:03.070 --> 00:06:04.640
Tell us! Tell us!

00:06:06.270 --> 00:06:09.970
<i>Alfredo spoke fervently for well over an hour.</i>

00:06:10.900 --> 00:06:14.200
<i>Their eyes were filled with respect for Alfredo,</i>

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:16.690
<i>...and their faces glowed with the joy of unity.</i>

00:06:17.360 --> 00:06:19.360
<i>Seeing the look in the eyes of his friends,</i>

00:06:19.800 --> 00:06:24.230
<i>...Romeo felt deeply ashamed for his childish outburst.</i>

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:30.800
So that's it... teamwork!

00:06:31.310 --> 00:06:32.630
Teamwork!

00:06:33.070 --> 00:06:35.560
The nail that sticks out and tries to act on his own is no good!

00:06:36.090 --> 00:06:39.620
The important thing is to pool your strength with everybody!

00:06:42.390 --> 00:06:45.630
Whatever happens, keep Alfredo at the center and back him up!

00:06:46.010 --> 00:06:46.980
Yeah!

00:06:51.230 --> 00:06:55.580
Hey... What's wrong, Romeo?
You haven't said a word all this time.

00:06:56.700 --> 00:06:58.290
It's nothing...!

00:06:58.770 --> 00:07:01.840
You didn't forget your bag and Piccolo, did you?

00:07:02.850 --> 00:07:03.640
Oh! Shoot!

00:07:03.930 --> 00:07:04.830
So long!

00:07:06.750 --> 00:07:09.200
Good luck! Good luck!

00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:39.810
Romeo!

00:07:41.070 --> 00:07:44.900
Alfredo... I'm embarrassed about how I behaved earlier...

00:07:46.580 --> 00:07:48.700
...acting stubborn like that...

00:07:52.620 --> 00:07:54.030
Don't worry about it!

00:07:58.810 --> 00:08:03.000
Knowing how to read a book like that, you're perfect as a leader!

00:08:03.220 --> 00:08:06.060
No way! There's still loads I don't understand in here.

00:08:08.530 --> 00:08:10.630
It's all falling to pieces.

00:08:10.830 --> 00:08:12.850
It's the only book I own.

00:08:16.450 --> 00:08:19.640
I've got it, Alfredo! Can you make a detour on your way home?

00:08:20.680 --> 00:08:22.820
I know a professor who gave me a book once.

00:08:23.190 --> 00:08:26.780
He might let you borrow a book, Alfredo!

00:08:30.220 --> 00:08:33.620
With pleasure! Any friend of yours is welcome, Romeo.

00:08:35.070 --> 00:08:37.800
I only hope you can find a book that will interest you, Alfredo.

00:08:38.640 --> 00:08:40.010
I'm Casera.

00:08:43.560 --> 00:08:45.430
Pleased to meet you, Professor Casera.

00:08:56.890 --> 00:08:59.210
Shakespeare! Goethe!

00:08:59.490 --> 00:09:01.760
Hmm! You seem to be well acquainted already.

00:09:06.640 --> 00:09:08.930
I've come to return your book, Professor.

00:09:11.460 --> 00:09:16.220
Phew! Voltaire is no easy read!

00:09:19.900 --> 00:09:22.240
Hey! That's not a book for kids to be reading!

00:09:22.920 --> 00:09:25.480
This is a book by Master Voltaire!

00:09:26.030 --> 00:09:27.950
Master Vol...taire...?

00:09:29.850 --> 00:09:33.220
He's the great man who taught our fatherland liberty and equality!

00:09:33.590 --> 00:09:35.990
Come on, hey, they're just kids.

00:09:36.350 --> 00:09:39.500
They won't understand what you mean by "liberty" and "equality".

00:09:40.400 --> 00:09:42.100
Isn't that right, flunky?

00:09:45.250 --> 00:09:46.730
Goodbye, Professor!

00:09:58.300 --> 00:10:00.660
Would you like to try to read it?

00:10:01.340 --> 00:10:02.930
Yes! Could I?

00:10:03.720 --> 00:10:07.560
Sure... but even college students find that a hard one...!

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:08.480
Yes!

00:10:10.640 --> 00:10:14.410
If, perchance, you should like to change it for another, come anytime.

00:10:14.830 --> 00:10:16.600
Thank you very much, Professor!

00:10:19.660 --> 00:10:23.380
What a mature boy he is!
Trying to read such a difficult book!

00:10:24.640 --> 00:10:26.270
How much older is he than you, Romeo?

00:10:26.690 --> 00:10:27.550
A year...

00:10:28.040 --> 00:10:30.680
Well! He seems much older than that!

00:10:31.580 --> 00:10:35.200
Compared with him, Romeo, why, you're still just a child!

00:10:41.480 --> 00:10:42.410
A child...

00:10:43.640 --> 00:10:46.570
Occasionally, you should challenge yourself.

00:10:47.260 --> 00:10:48.450
Yes, I will.

00:10:48.930 --> 00:10:51.820
Right. Then take your time and read at your leisure.

00:11:04.910 --> 00:11:07.290
Am I really... a child?

00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:46.550
I think by now you should be able to read this book, Romeo.

00:11:50.930 --> 00:11:54.770
I'll set my goal... to be like Alfredo!

00:12:15.050 --> 00:12:16.000
Romeo was?!

00:12:16.190 --> 00:12:18.460
Yes, I tell you.
He was reading a book!

00:12:20.580 --> 00:12:23.420
Have you guys ever read a book?

00:12:23.690 --> 00:12:25.250
I can't even read!

00:12:30.870 --> 00:12:37.440
Lessee... Do.. Donk...
Donkey! That's it!

00:12:37.620 --> 00:12:39.210
I got it... finally!

00:12:41.300 --> 00:12:43.750
Whoa! He really is reading!

00:12:44.720 --> 00:12:46.150
Wh... What?!

00:12:48.130 --> 00:12:49.940
What's this!?
It's a pig!

00:12:51.110 --> 00:12:56.950
It's not a pig! It's a donkey, from Aesop's Fables...!

00:12:57.280 --> 00:12:58.340
What's the story about?

00:12:59.530 --> 00:13:02.220
Uh... well...

00:13:02.480 --> 00:13:05.320
I know what it's about!
I saw it at the puppet show!

00:13:05.680 --> 00:13:09.380
Oink! Oink! Oink! Oink!

00:13:09.820 --> 00:13:13.940
Pig stories! So that's the kind of "book" you read!

00:13:14.250 --> 00:13:15.490
Oink! Oink!

00:13:17.780 --> 00:13:19.100
It's a donkey!

00:13:19.610 --> 00:13:22.140
Hey! Let me tell you what happens at the end!

00:13:22.270 --> 00:13:24.130
Don't! I'd like to read it.

00:13:24.350 --> 00:13:26.550
At the end...!
At the end...!!

00:13:26.710 --> 00:13:28.510
I said don't tell me!

00:13:28.780 --> 00:13:31.330
Everybody lives happily ever after!

00:13:34.160 --> 00:13:35.740
That's it!
Now I'm mad!

00:13:35.870 --> 00:13:39.000
So that's it...! Happily ever after!

00:13:39.250 --> 00:13:40.080
Dante...!

00:13:41.210 --> 00:13:43.190
I'm through with you guys!

00:13:43.880 --> 00:13:45.040
So leave me alone!

00:13:49.890 --> 00:13:51.220
<i>Let them laugh all they want...</i>

00:13:51.570 --> 00:13:53.160
<i>I'm still going to read it through to the end!</i>

00:13:56.510 --> 00:13:59.260
<i>I'm not going to lose to Alfredo!</i>

00:14:00.380 --> 00:14:01.530
Alfredo!

00:14:04.880 --> 00:14:08.010
Why you... are you reading again? This trash!

00:14:08.740 --> 00:14:09.420
Give it back!

00:14:12.840 --> 00:14:14.140
Stuff and nonsense, books!

00:14:14.400 --> 00:14:16.360
Do some work if you've got time to burn for reading!

00:14:25.360 --> 00:14:27.430
Go and prepare dinner!
And I mean now!

00:14:35.920 --> 00:14:38.050
Uhm... I'll go back to my room.

00:14:38.140 --> 00:14:41.250
Already?
- It's late...

00:14:41.710 --> 00:14:42.770
Romeo...!

00:14:43.390 --> 00:14:43.780
Hm?

00:14:44.160 --> 00:14:46.280
You've been acting fidgety lately...

00:14:46.780 --> 00:14:48.720
...going back to your room in a hurry like that...

00:14:49.120 --> 00:14:51.210
No, I haven't, I don't think!

00:14:51.540 --> 00:14:52.400
And...

00:14:52.670 --> 00:14:53.040
Eh?

00:14:54.700 --> 00:14:56.570
You've never once asked me to give you a reading lesson.

00:14:57.030 --> 00:14:58.950
Oh... I haven't...?

00:14:59.060 --> 00:15:01.200
Gee, I've been so busy lately with this thing and all...

00:15:01.590 --> 00:15:02.450
"This thing"?

00:15:03.620 --> 00:15:08.850
You'll be the first to know it... when the donkeys live happily ever after!

00:15:08.960 --> 00:15:10.210
Donkeys?

00:15:10.610 --> 00:15:11.310
Good night!

00:15:16.690 --> 00:15:18.350
<i>I'm sorry, Angeletta!</i>

00:15:18.960 --> 00:15:22.140
<i>But just this once, I want to...</i>

00:15:53.880 --> 00:15:57.120
And just... just then, the robber...

00:15:57.360 --> 00:15:58.570
Oh, man, this is no good...

00:15:59.170 --> 00:16:03.000
Piccolo! Wake me up if I start falling asleep, would you?!

00:16:08.180 --> 00:16:13.030
...the robber flopped backwards onto his back!

00:17:18.010 --> 00:17:19.050
Big brother!

00:17:28.550 --> 00:17:29.580
<i>Bianca!</i>

00:17:38.930 --> 00:17:43.820
You said you'd watch me dance!
And there you sit reading a book!

00:17:44.370 --> 00:17:46.820
Stay by my side for ever and ever!

00:18:05.640 --> 00:18:10.870
I'll become an adult quickly! ...build my knowledge, and my strength!

00:18:11.770 --> 00:18:15.890
And I'll come to take you away, Bianca!

00:18:27.990 --> 00:18:31.830
Then... you read it, this book here?

00:18:32.330 --> 00:18:32.890
Yes.

00:18:33.130 --> 00:18:34.760
And that fast?

00:18:35.840 --> 00:18:37.620
But... I'm sorry.

00:18:38.930 --> 00:18:42.890
Two pages got burned.

00:18:52.220 --> 00:18:52.750
What's this?

00:18:53.380 --> 00:18:56.100
I wrote down the sentences I could remember from those two pages.

00:18:57.330 --> 00:19:03.520
You mean you remembered every sentence from those two pages?

00:19:04.910 --> 00:19:08.350
They were so wonderful... I was reading them over again and again...

00:19:09.100 --> 00:19:13.600
Thank you very much, Professor!
I'm very excited right now!

00:19:14.790 --> 00:19:19.640
I don't know how to express it properly... but... I can hardly sleep!

00:19:19.880 --> 00:19:23.010
The liberty and equality in those pages has taught me something...

00:19:31.120 --> 00:19:33.240
It's nearly word-for-word the same as the original.

00:19:35.090 --> 00:19:38.990
<i>God puts special talents on this earth sometimes.</i>

00:19:40.270 --> 00:19:44.520
<i>That boy is surely blessed in the eyes of our Lord.</i>

00:19:47.540 --> 00:19:52.460
<i>As an adult, he could make great changes in the world.</i>

00:20:21.130 --> 00:20:23.140
Only one more page left 'till the end!

00:20:26.380 --> 00:20:32.880
And... everybody lived happily ever after.

00:20:37.770 --> 00:20:39.850
I did it! Angeletta!

00:20:39.910 --> 00:20:42.120
I finished reading! The donkeys lived happily ever after!

00:20:43.880 --> 00:20:45.000
Angeletta!

00:20:59.840 --> 00:21:02.310
Everybody's living happily now.

00:21:09.780 --> 00:21:13.480
<i>Romeo had discovered the joy of finishing a book.</i>

00:21:29.880 --> 00:21:34.580
<i>So Alfredo's torch of learning was passed on to Romeo,</i>

00:21:35.210 --> 00:21:39.180
<i>...ultimately leading him towards a certain occupation.</i>

00:21:39.890 --> 00:21:46.980
<i>But, he could not even imagine such a future yet.</i>

00:21:56.330 --> 00:21:59.220
<i>The Wolf Pack doesn't even pretend to stop picking on the weak.</i>

00:21:59.750 --> 00:22:01.180
<i>We can't just continue running away!</i>

00:22:01.950 --> 00:22:04.400
<i>So we initiated a secret plan!</i>

00:22:05.260 --> 00:22:07.170
<i>We're through letting you off foot-loose and fancy-free!</i>

00:22:08.280 --> 00:22:12.050
See you then!

00:22:08.280 --> 00:22:12.050
<i>Showdown at San Babila Church</i>

00:22:08.280 --> 00:22:12.050
Next time:

00:22:14.090 --> 00:22:18.090
<i>"Si Si Ciao ~ On These Roman Roofs"</i>

00:22:26.700 --> 00:22:30.800
<i>Si Si Ciao, why do the good times</i>

00:22:30.900 --> 00:22:35.100
<i>seem to end so soon?</i>

00:22:35.300 --> 00:22:39.300
<i>Si Si Ciao, we're all friends</i>

00:22:39.500 --> 00:22:43.500
<i>Let's meet again on these Roman roofs</i>

00:22:44.110 --> 00:22:48.410
<i>Your laughing voice dances</i>

00:22:48.410 --> 00:22:52.310
<i>Once again in the sky</i>

00:22:52.710 --> 00:22:59.610
<i>Your pocket bursting with memories</i>

00:23:01.310 --> 00:23:05.210
<i>Si Si Ciao, goodbye but for now</i>

00:23:05.410 --> 00:23:09.410
<i>Let's meet again on these Roman roofs</i>
